cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23085093
title: "How accurate is altitude from pressure geolocators? Code and data for a global assessment of three pressure-to-altitude conversions"
abstract: >-
  Global assessment of three pressure-to-altitude conversions: a fixed standard atmosphere,
  ERA5 surface conditions with a standard lapse rate, and ERA5 with virtual temperature and
  a GPT3 lapse rate. References are GHCNh weather stations and IGRA2 radiosondes evaluated
  up to 5 km above the launch surface, using qualifying 12-month windows within 2022–2026.
  The study quantifies absolute errors, station bias and within-station variability, compares
  ERA5 with ERA5-Land, and assesses sensitivity to atmospheric query location.
